<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('partials/head') %></head>
<body data-page="home">
<%- include('partials/intro') %>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

<main id="main">

<section class="hero" id="heroCarousel">
  <div class="hero-bg active" id="heroBgA"></div>
  <div class="hero-bg" id="heroBgB"></div>
  <div class="wrap" id="heroWrapA"></div>
  <div class="wrap" id="heroWrapB"></div>
  <button class="hero-arrow left" id="heroPrev" aria-label="Previous highlight">‹</button>
  <button class="hero-arrow right" id="heroNext" aria-label="Next highlight">›</button>
  <div class="hero-dots" id="heroDots"></div>
</section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap grid grid-feature">
      <div class="card reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Est. 1948</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;"><span id="icsoYears" data-count="<%= icsoYears %>">0</span> years as Imperial's flagship orchestra</h3>
        <p>Conducted by Oliver Gooch, the Imperial College Symphony Orchestra (ICSO) has served as the flagship orchestra of Imperial College London since 1948. Within the UK's only exclusively STEMB university, ICSO offers a fully auditioned, premier creative outlet for dedicated Imperial musicians (some with scholarships for lessons at the Royal College of Music) to deliver impactful, high-calibre performances to sold-out audiences across London and attracting interest abroad on international tours. Highlights from 2025-26 range from concertos by Dvořák (Robyn Liu, cello) and Korngold (Kaelyn Soh, violin), to Tchaikovsky's <i>Romeo and Juliet Fantasy Overture</i>, Shostakovich's <i>Symphony No. 9</i>, and Britten's monumental <i>War Requiem</i>.</p>
        <img src="/assets/strings-rach-prok-2025.jpg" alt="ICSO performing in concert" class="feature-card-photo">
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Prizes</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;">Awards and recognition</h3>
        <p>Having won "Universiy Orchestra of the Year" (2008) and with a BAFTA-awarded TV debut on Channel 4 (2002), ICSO is widely regarded as one of the finest university orchestras in the UK.</p>
        <p>ICSO's recognition is also highlighted the words of Daniel Jemison (LSO Principal Bassoon), who has previously described ICSO as sounding "like a professional orchestra".</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">In London and going abroad</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;">Cadogan Hall, London, and abroad</h3>
        <p>ICSO holds its annual Spring Concert at Cadogan Hall, a top orchestral venue and home of the RPO. Additionally, ICSO recently performed in Imperial's Great Hall, RCM's Amaryllis Fleming Hall, and Windsor Castle. International tours held by ICSO have also led the orchestra beyond the UK, to Spain, South Africa, Italy, Finland, Czechia, and Belgium.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- <hr class="divider"> -->

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <!-- <p class="eyebrow">Watch</p> -->
        <h2>ICSO at Cadogan Hall</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="media-slot reveal" id="watchVideo" data-video-id="-f0cP-uu2Wo"></div>
      <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:.85rem;color:var(--ink-soft);text-align:center;font-style:italic;">ICSO performing Rachmaninoff's Piano Concerto No. 3 (Bendit Chan, piano) and Prokofiev's Symphony No. 5 at Cadogan Hall (March 2025)</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>

<script>
const heroSlides = [
  { img:'/assets/ghent.jpg', eyebrow:'Past highlight • June 2026', title:'ICSO Tour to<br>Ghent, Belgium', lede:"ICSO and Sinfonietta teamed up with London-based, Belgian, and Spanish university orchestras for two concerts in Ghent amidst the June heatwave. Programmed fiery Spanish works from Giminéz & Rimsky-Korsakov, and featured 4th-year biomedical engineer Robyn Liu in Dvořák's Cello Concerto." },
  { img:'/assets/war-requiem-2026.jpg', eyebrow:'Past highlight • 28 February 2026', title:"Benjamin Britten's<br>War Requiem", lede:"As part of the Windsor Festival, an extended ICSO joins with Imperial College Choirs, Coventry Cathedral Chorus, Orpheus Sinfonia, the Choristers of St George's Chapel and several solo voices for an anniversary performance of Britten's pacifist masterwork in St George's Chapel, Windsor Castle." }
];
window.__heroSlides = heroSlides;
</script>
</body>
</html>
